WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.491 --> 00:00:02.717
(audience cheers)
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.717 --> 00:00:03.550
- [Kelly] It's been a minute!

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.350
You were here a bit ago.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.830
- Yeah, and actually, it
was during COVID, remember?

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:08.820
- That,
- [Kelly] I know.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.653
- It was like a sci-fi,
- The screen.

00:00:09.653 --> 00:00:11.077
- Yeah, the screens.
- Yes.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.197
That was when I talked to
everybody via a screen.

00:00:13.197 --> 00:00:14.030
- Yeah, exactly.
- Yes.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.630
I like you physically in person more.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.787
- Absolutely, yeah.
- Yes.

00:00:16.787 --> 00:00:18.949
- We can like, touch.
- Thank you, yeah, yeah.

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:20.488
- So good to see the audience.

00:00:20.488 --> 00:00:21.357
- So wait, it's New Year's now.

00:00:21.357 --> 00:00:22.950
So what do y'all do in Venezuela?

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.189
Do you have any, like,
special things y'all do?

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:27.269
- In Venezuela many,

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:29.130
there is one that I used to do

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.597
when I was a kid.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.917
- And it really paid off.
- [Kelly] What?

00:00:32.917 --> 00:00:34.950
- You go around, I mean,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.200
when the clock hits 00:00

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.230
you hug everybody and
then you take a suitcase

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.760
and go around the block,

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.930
running around the block,

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:46.050
and that will give you a lot of travels.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:46.950
You know,

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:47.940
during the year.
- [Kelly] I like this.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.230
- So I did it a lot when I was a kid

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.520
and now I'm traveling all the time.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.408
- You're traveling all the time, it works!

00:00:51.408 --> 00:00:52.770
Do it, kids!
- That's what it pays off.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:53.790
- Do it.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.208
There's something with
grapes, as well, right?

00:00:56.208 --> 00:00:57.041
- Oh, yeah.
- Because I think

00:00:57.041 --> 00:00:57.874
they do the same thing in Mexico.

00:00:57.874 --> 00:00:59.200
'Cause I was in Mexico
once and they were like,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.170
all of a sudden, there
were grapes at the table,

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:02.190
and I think they do the same thing

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.532
in Venezuela.
- The same thing.

00:01:03.532 --> 00:01:05.130
- [Kelly] I had no idea.
- So it is 12 grapes

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.930
for the months of the year.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:07.990
It's 12 months, right?
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:09.059
Yeah, of course.

00:01:09.059 --> 00:01:10.373
- There are 12 months.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:10.373 --> 00:01:11.880
So it's 12 wishes.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:12.713
- Yeah.

00:01:12.713 --> 00:01:15.030
- And then right before
the clock hits 00:00,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.620
then you have to eat them.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.030
- [Kelly] Yes.
- And make a wish

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.863
for each grape.

00:01:18.863 --> 00:01:19.696
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:19.696 --> 00:01:21.210
- I thought whenever I was doing it,

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.220
I heard someone,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.990
'cause I was drinking tequila.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.977
- Yeah, of course.
- And I heard them say,

00:01:26.977 --> 00:01:28.860
"You have to eat it in the first minute."

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:29.693
- Yeah.

00:01:29.693 --> 00:01:32.430
- But I think it's actually
have to eat them each minute.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.840
Like the first 12 minutes.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.460
So I was like, just, just,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.589
I wanted my wishes to come true.

00:01:37.589 --> 00:01:38.917
- [Edgar] I was just like you.

00:01:38.917 --> 00:01:40.337
- I ate them so fast.
- Yeah, I would always do it

00:01:40.337 --> 00:01:42.180
in the 12 seconds before.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.013
- Yeah, I did it.

00:01:43.013 --> 00:01:44.160
Yeah, somebody was like, no, no, no.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.390
It was, like, one a minute.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.460
And I was, like, "No, I didn't hear that."

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.410
Anyway, I got my wishes, though.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.539
So there you go.
- [Edgar] Yeah.

00:01:50.539 --> 00:01:51.888
(audience cheering)

00:01:51.888 --> 00:01:53.250
- [Kelly] Well, speaking of travel,

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.140
Edgar actually recently went to Croatia,

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.310
so here's a video.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.930
- [Kelly] What's happening man?

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.763
- [Edgar] Oh my God.

00:01:58.763 --> 00:01:59.700
- [Kelly] What is this dance?

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.283
- [Edgar] If I only knew
what was happening there.

00:02:03.645 --> 00:02:05.169
- [Kelly] I feel like I did
this in show choir once.

00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:09.090
- [Edgar] I ended up on a
boat with a bunch of Croatian

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.170
and Bosnian people

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.480
and then suddenly, they played that music.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.508
They started to dance
and I just joined in.

00:02:14.508 --> 00:02:15.341
- [Kelly] I like it.

00:02:15.341 --> 00:02:16.174
- So yeah.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:16.174 --> 00:02:17.329
- It's like a folk.
- [Kelly] It feels good.

00:02:17.329 --> 00:02:18.270
- Yeah, it feels good, yeah.
- I like jumping.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:19.518
It's good for lymphatic system.

00:02:19.518 --> 00:02:20.351
- [Edgar] Yeah.

00:02:20.351 --> 00:02:21.184
- It's perfect.
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:21.184 --> 00:02:22.710
- Do you like dancing in general?

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.289
- Yeah, I'm from Venezuela so, yeah.

00:02:24.289 --> 00:02:26.087
- He said, "Yes, yes."

00:02:26.087 --> 00:02:27.049
I love dancing.

00:02:27.049 --> 00:02:27.882
- [Edgar] Yeah, I love dancing too.

00:02:27.882 --> 00:02:29.040
- Makes me feel so good.
- Yeah.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.840
- [Kelly] Okay, we have
something else in common.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.308
You love collecting watches.

00:02:32.308 --> 00:02:33.141
- [Edgar] Yeah, I do.

00:02:33.141 --> 00:02:34.695
- Yeah, so I love giving watches.

00:02:34.695 --> 00:02:35.528
- [Edgar] Okay.

00:02:35.528 --> 00:02:36.660
- As a gift, 'cause I
don't wear them generally,

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.867
but I love -
- It's Christmas.

00:02:37.867 --> 00:02:38.700
- [Kelly] Okay, okay.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.050
I'm just saying I love watches.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.330
I don't actually like knowing the time,

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.550
which is weird because it rushes me

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:45.540
and I wanna live my life.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.920
But I love watches.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.120
Like the art of them are so beautiful.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:48.953
- Yeah, I mean, what you love,

00:02:48.953 --> 00:02:50.340
what you love is,

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.548
is the beauty of the watches.
- Yeah.

00:02:51.548 --> 00:02:52.590
- It's almost like jewelry.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.990
- And you're right, I always
get 'em like engraved,

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.130
like with a little message when I give,

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:56.963
yeah.

00:02:56.963 --> 00:02:57.796
- [Edgar] Ah, that's very cute.

00:02:57.796 --> 00:02:58.767
- So you collect them, right?

00:02:58.767 --> 00:02:59.600
- [Edgar] I collect, yeah.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:00.450
I mean, I used to say

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.220
that I had a watch collection,

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.790
but actually now it's my
dad's watch collection,

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.107
'cause every time he
comes visit and he says,

00:03:08.107 --> 00:03:09.868
"Oh, that watch so cute, can I have it?"

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:10.897
(audience laughs)
- Takes your watch.

00:03:10.897 --> 00:03:12.240
- [Edgar] Oh, it's so cute,
can I use it for a little bit?

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.740
And then he just takes it home, so now,

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:14.573
- [Kelly] You and your
father have a collection.

00:03:14.573 --> 00:03:16.038
- [Edgar] So now it's like,
our watch collection, yeah.

00:03:16.038 --> 00:03:16.871
- Yeah.

00:03:16.871 --> 00:03:17.704
- [Edgar] It used to be mine,

00:03:17.704 --> 00:03:18.537
but now, well.

00:03:18.537 --> 00:03:19.370
- [Kelly] I love.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.203
- It's gonna be mine anyway.

00:03:20.203 --> 00:03:21.036
- [Kelly] Do you get into pocket watches?

00:03:21.036 --> 00:03:21.869
That's what I'm obsessed
with, specifically.

00:03:21.869 --> 00:03:22.769
- [Edgar] Pocket watches, I don't know.

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:23.878
- I just think they're
so cool with the chain.

00:03:23.878 --> 00:03:25.013
- But the ones that you,
with the chain, oh no,

00:03:25.013 --> 00:03:27.180
I have, well, I should,
I should look into that.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.110
- Oh, man.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:28.943
- Yeah.

00:03:28.943 --> 00:03:29.776
- They're really cool.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:30.609
- Yeah.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:32.040
- But they're, but you do, but you do,

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:32.940
- [Kelly] Look, I tried,

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:33.900
- But you have the chain, right?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.060
- Well, I give them as
gifts like a lot of times.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.140
Like I've, or I've done it a few,

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.610
yeah, they're very cool.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.443
- Yeah.

00:03:39.443 --> 00:03:40.710
- Do you have significance
behind this watch?

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.300
- [Edgar] Yeah, I mean, it was a gift.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.253
- Oh.

00:03:43.253 --> 00:03:44.370
- It was a gift for, for a very, you know,

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.870
special premiere at the, you know,

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.100
Cannes Film Festival in France.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:47.933
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:47.933 --> 00:03:49.710
- And then I had this big movie

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.580
and I walk up this, you
know, the red carpet,

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.413
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:53.413 --> 00:03:54.246
The stairs, yeah.

00:03:54.246 --> 00:03:55.230
- It was pretty, yeah,
it was pretty, you know,

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.540
it's a, it's a beautiful
life, you know that we have

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.793
- Yes, very blessed.

00:03:58.793 --> 00:03:59.640
- [Edgar] It's like a reminder of

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.190
that maybe some things
have been done well.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.023
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:03.023 --> 00:04:04.860
- You know, so it's like, I don't know.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:05.693
- [Kelly] You did some things right?

00:04:05.693 --> 00:04:06.526
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:06.526 --> 00:04:07.359
- Yeah exactly, so.

00:04:07.359 --> 00:04:08.192
- Yeah, I love that.

00:04:08.192 --> 00:04:09.690
I don't like anything unless
there's meaning behind it.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:10.680
I like a meaning.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:11.653
- [Edgar] Yeah, totally.

00:04:11.653 --> 00:04:12.690
- Because I'm not really
materialistic in general.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.523
- No, no, no.

00:04:13.523 --> 00:04:14.550
It's how, how the intention

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:17.118
is bound to the to the object.

00:04:17.118 --> 00:04:17.951
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:17.951 --> 00:04:18.784
- It's not the object on, on itself.

00:04:18.784 --> 00:04:19.617
- [Kelly] Yeah, agreed.

00:04:19.617 --> 00:04:21.120
- It's the memories and what, you know,

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:21.953
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:04:21.953 --> 00:04:23.310
- The beautiful memories
that they bring to you.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.143
- [Kelly] I agree.

00:04:24.143 --> 00:04:25.460
That's why I like tattoos as well.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.293
- [Edgar] Yeah.

00:04:26.293 --> 00:04:27.126
- I'm covered.

00:04:27.126 --> 00:04:28.860
- I don't have, I, yeah,
I don't have tattoos.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:29.693
- [Kelly] Oh, man.

00:04:29.693 --> 00:04:30.526
- At all.

00:04:30.526 --> 00:04:31.500
I haven't found like an image to.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.150
- [Kelly] Don't, if you
find one, don't worry,

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:34.320
then you'll find 20 more.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.153
- [Edgar] That's what happens, yeah.

00:04:35.153 --> 00:04:36.030
- Yeah, You get one

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:37.590
and then you're like, this is fun,

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:38.522
and then.

00:04:38.522 --> 00:04:39.355
- [Edgar] Yeah, yeah.

00:04:39.355 --> 00:04:40.188
- I mean, mine are all memories,
the same kind of thing.

00:04:40.188 --> 00:04:42.150
Mine are all, you know,
places and things and that.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.740
- And you can look at all of them, or?

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:44.760
- No, not the one,

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.340
I often forget there's one
on my back right shoulder,

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.173
I forgot.

00:04:48.173 --> 00:04:49.006
And I got that in Amsterdam.

00:04:49.006 --> 00:04:49.839
I was not high.

00:04:49.839 --> 00:04:50.709
- Okay.

00:04:50.709 --> 00:04:51.542
(everyone laughs)

00:04:51.542 --> 00:04:53.070
- I got it because there's Hanky there.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:55.230
He did a lot of us on tour
when we were there touring.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.897
And I was like, and it hurt.

00:04:56.897 --> 00:04:58.320
(Kelly chuckles)

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:01.382
But I did it, and it's big, but anyway.

00:05:01.382 --> 00:05:03.750
So I heard that you were
a journalist at one point.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:04.583
- Yeah, I was a journalist before.

00:05:04.583 --> 00:05:07.380
- So what, when did that
career switch happen?

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.390
- Well, you know what,

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:10.980
and that brings me back to the,

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:12.900
to the New Year's tradition.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.042
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:14.042 --> 00:05:15.420
- I always wanted, I
always wanted to travel.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.370
That was, I wanted to be a journalist

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.860
so that I could get,
become a international

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.068
correspondent so that I could travel.

00:05:22.068 --> 00:05:22.901
- Yeah.

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:24.810
- And I always, and I also
wanted to be a diplomat,

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.520
'cause my dad was a military attache

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.380
and sort of like a military diplomat.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:29.213
- Yeah.

00:05:29.213 --> 00:05:31.620
- So I wanted to do something in life

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:32.820
that would allow me to travel

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:34.350
and get to know interesting people

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.210
and have great conversations.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.043
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:37.043 --> 00:05:37.876
- And that's pretty much what I'm doing.

00:05:37.876 --> 00:05:39.390
- [Kelly] I was like, both
those jobs entail that.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:40.656
- [Edgar] Exactly, so then,

00:05:40.656 --> 00:05:43.350
there was something that happens

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.630
towards my last year at University.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.600
A friend of mine invited
me to do a short film.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.160
And then I said, but I'm not an actor.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.037
And I said, well, but I
need like, someone like you.

00:05:51.037 --> 00:05:55.405
It's like an experimental
abstract, weird short film.

00:05:55.405 --> 00:05:56.238
- Wait, they called.

00:05:56.238 --> 00:05:57.071
Oh, I thought that he was saying,

00:05:57.071 --> 00:05:58.696
I need someone like you, weird, abstract.

00:05:58.696 --> 00:06:01.020
I thought he was describing the character.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.325
- Yeah, exactly like with
a comma or a big comma,

00:06:02.325 --> 00:06:03.690
weird like that.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:04.523
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:06:04.523 --> 00:06:07.725
- Someone like you, comma weird, abstract.

00:06:07.725 --> 00:06:10.050
And all I had to do was just to make out

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.376
with this girl in a latex suit.

00:06:12.376 --> 00:06:13.209
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:06:13.209 --> 00:06:14.445
In a latex suit?

00:06:14.445 --> 00:06:16.260
- Yeah, they bleached my hair.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.033
I know that's gonna, that's gonna bite me.

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:18.866
- [Kelly] I wanna,

00:06:18.866 --> 00:06:20.354
I wanna find this.

00:06:20.354 --> 00:06:21.540
- [Edgar] That's gonna come back to me.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:22.569
- Yeah.

00:06:22.569 --> 00:06:23.402
- [Edgar] Soon, I don't know.

00:06:23.402 --> 00:06:24.714
Well, but yes, that exists somewhere.

00:06:24.714 --> 00:06:25.547
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:06:25.547 --> 00:06:28.320
- And then it turned out to be a quite,

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.210
you know, apparently decent short film.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.800
And then it got selected in a

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.200
film festival for students.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.033
- You got the bug.

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.720
- And then one thing led to another.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.576
And then here I am
talking to Kelly Clarkson.

00:06:38.576 --> 00:06:40.365
- Yeah and you're so good.

00:06:40.365 --> 00:06:41.198
(audience applauds)

00:06:41.198 --> 00:06:42.031
- You're such a great actor.

00:06:42.031 --> 00:06:42.960
It's so interesting that you haven't

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.520
had that dream, like, since you're a kid,

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:45.810
'cause you're so good at it.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:46.643
- [Edgar] Thank you so much.

